# Draconic Visitor's replacement ("If one or more artifact tokens would be created under your control, that many 5/5 red
# Dragon creature tokens with flying are created instead") sees a token as it would be created, not as it would enter the
# battlefield. Its ruling (2026-08-21): "If you create a nonartifact token that will be an artifact as it enters the
# battlefield, such as a token that will be an artifact because of Mycosynth Lattice, Draconic Visitor's effect doesn't
# apply to that token's creation" - the Visitor modifies how tokens are created, the Lattice applies only once they are
# entering. So CR 614.12's look-ahead, which counts continuous effects already in place, is not what the Visitor asks.
# Bot1 casts Mycosynth Lattice (turn 1), Draconic Visitor (turn 3) and Command the Stage (turn 5): its colorless Cadet is
# created as it is, enters as an artifact (the Lattice), and no Dragon token is made.
# (draconic-visitor-turns-a-blood-token-into-a-dragon is the control: a token that is an artifact as created.)

